{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/896510-the-creepiest-disturbing-bloodline","id":896510,"title":"The Creepiest/Disturbing Bloodline?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-22T21:19:42-07:00","id":896510,"title":"The Creepiest/Disturbing Bloodline?","content":"What is the creepiest and the most disturbing bloodline in Requiem that is to the point that they're best served as NPCs, Urban Legends and even antagonists but not as PCs?<br /> <br /> As for me it has to be Macellarius which they're just....ugh and also the Oberlochs which their &quot;eternal youth&quot; feature pretty much gets much thrown out of the window although they do serve some inspiration of a similar weakness where the Vampire not only grows old, they also start to decay as well till the point they literally become walking corpses which would resemble Liches with Fangs but I don't think it's the case with the Oberlochs though....<br /> <br /> Can anyone else point out anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","user":"spaceharrier72","date":". 05-23-2016, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T21:20:22-07:00","id":897549,"title":"","content":"I think the Oberloch was going for something like Grandpa Sawyer.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/texaschainsawmassacre/images/5/5a/Leatherface_Texas_Chainsaw_Massacre_III_9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Part of the problem with questions like these is that the clan and even bloodline aren't really the determining factors when it comes to how creepy or disturbing a vampire is. Justin Bieber could be kidnapped and Embraced by Oberlochs tomorrow night, and would be far less creepy than Grandpa Sawyer. For a while, at least. And providing you don't find him creepy or disturbing to begin with.<br /> <br /> All that said, if I had to pick one, it would be House Telamones, from Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners. They are a very insular and unique bloodline, and their appearance drastically changes them from the way an ordinary human looks. In addition to their overall appearance, including the gaining of some physical deformities, their culture is a bizarre and tyrannical system that manages to go against a lot of vampire instincts. The bloodline is ruled by Overseers. Every century, these Overseers pick two heirs from among their bloodline. These two commit diablerie on the Overseers and become the new Overseers for the next hundred years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-24-2016, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T21:40:32-07:00","id":897563,"title":"","content":"The Formosae from Wicked Dead make me sick. I have yet to read a description of a Namtaru's Horror that has the same effect on me as them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:06:49-07:00","id":897924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/896510-the-creepiest-disturbing-bloodline?p=897549#post897549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said, if I had to pick one, it would be House Telamones, from Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners. They are a very insular and unique bloodline, and their appearance drastically changes them from the way an ordinary human looks. In addition to their overall appearance, including the gaining of some physical deformities, their culture is a bizarre and tyrannical system that manages to go against a lot of vampire instincts. The bloodline is ruled by Overseers. Every century, these Overseers pick two heirs from among their bloodline. These two commit diablerie on the Overseers and become the new Overseers for the next hundred years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sound like the Telamones could easily translate to Masquerade style Nosferatu but their deformity curse is much more in a slower pace than rapidly like the latter....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11735-spaceharrier72","name":"spaceharrier72","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:59:42-07:00","id":898261,"title":"","content":"The Melisiade and all their drone-style brainwashing and mind control. I find them excedingly creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982